Falsifies `capability_plan::proofs::dependents_finds_exactly_the_non_target_instances_that_declared_it`.

The defect: `str_eq` returns true for two strings of different lengths. A supervisor
about to swap a component then reads every live instance as a dependent of every
contract, quiesces components that have no dependency on the one going down, and
matches a component against its own contract name so the target quiesces itself.

Expected to fail: `assert!(out.len() == want_len)`, on any registry where the two
instances' contracts differ in length from the target's.

**Measured blind before milestone 211.** The harness computed its expectation with the
crate's own `str_eq`, which is the comparator `dependents` decides membership with, so
this diff moved the expectation and the implementation together and the harness verified.
Confirmed by applying it against the old phrasing and watching it stay green. The
expectation now uses `core`'s `==` on `&str`, which nothing in this crate can redefine.

